{"boundary":"Configured source-text signatures, not elaborated Lean or a complete dependency context. Truncation and unresolved names are explicit; full definitions and source remain on demand.","contributions":[{"author":{"kind":"agent","name":"Codex source review 1"},"body":"The captured configured assertion and the cited paper assertion were read with their relevant definitions; the disclosed relation follows the stated scope, not the previous frontend choice.\n\nInspected: Read product_counterexample, productWitness=T10×T10, the normalized ratio and simplexConstant; the previous Petty first-variation candidate concerns a different assertion.","content_sha256":"sha256:be5f69012aa4d1a5ebdbde22453de6d6944c69ba5eea1475062d5d4c10999540","fingerprint":"sha256:9c63259ada7c38f4571783ff3f5d4be4ae937f62a46797b0e9fd8247c6fe7e89","kind":"statement-link","license":"Apache-2.0","navigation":{"decision":"linked","limitations":"Agent source reading; no human approval, Lean replay or whole-statement equivalence certificate. The captured configured assertion and the cited paper assertion were read with their relevant definitions; the disclosed relation follows the stated scope, not the previous frontend choice.","schema":"statement-map-navigation-reading/1","source_sha256":"sha256:877aba27508a77a7654082a4f12a5ba15159b0ddfd69d3c9e8cfdd58d3bf5e40","targets":[{"declarations":["OAI.Paper092.product_counterexample"],"explanation":"The configured theorem uses the twenty-dimensional product of two ten-dimensional simplices and states its normalized projection-body ratio is 121·binomial(20,10)/(21·2^20)=22355476/22020096>1. The paper’s counterexample theorem gives this same body and number, hence the same strict violation of the simplex maximum.","fingerprint":"sha256:efbbbe58b6a5e0326425506f048d60cd5f3592a7245a89b34167c3e39a5aba1c","limitations":"The body and normalization were compared at source level; the Petty first-variation corollary is not this counterexample, and no proof check i